    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="1098" n="992" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg992"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39) City of Flint/34: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-26T00:00:00+03:00">October 26,
                            1939—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received October 26—6:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>808. My 807, October 26, 11 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">p.m.</hi>]. The Soviet
                    radio at 11:30 p.m., announced that after examination of her cargo the naval
                    authorities have decided to release the <hi rendition="#italic">City of
                        Flint</hi> on condition that she leave the port of Murmansk immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
